<!--
    Launcher foreground: the cits-to-go logo, the icon of the identity package kept in
    images/app-icon.svg, without its cream tile. The paths take the 750 px coordinates
    and the stroke widths of that file, each bezier segment with its own command letter.

    Geometry of the logo: the C is an arc of radius 210 about (356.25, 375), open from
    -58 degrees to +58 degrees, drawn as a 120 wide dark green road with a 66 wide
    lighter green centre and a dashed cream centre line. The signal is concentric at
    (442.5, 375): a dot of radius 34.5 in a 33 wide stroke, so an amber ring, and three
    waves of radius 93.75, 150 and 210, each 31.5 wide and open 80 degrees; the outer one
    has the radius of the road.

    The ink reaches 293.25 px from the tile centre (375, 375), at the right end of the
    outer wave. The group moves that centre to the canvas centre (54, 54) and scales by
    0.1105, so the ink fills a circle of radius 32.4 dp, inside the 33 dp radius of the
    adaptive icon safe zone.

    Vector drawables have no stroke dashes, so the dashed centre line is twelve separate
    9 degree arcs, the first at 60 degrees and the next every 21 degrees.
-->
